;; profiles.edn — how a role RUNS. Never what it may do.
;;
;; ## Why this is separate from everything else here
;;
;; `businesses.edn` says which roles exist. `yakuwari/` says what each role is
;; for and what it may do alone. `fleet.edn` bounds how many run at once.
;; None of them say which model answers, or on whose subscription.
;;
;; That was not a gap anyone declared — it was a constant. cloud-itonami-app
;; wrote `:bot/provider-id "murakumo"` and `:bot/model "murakumo-main"` as
;; literals at provisioning time, so all 90 Bots were identical because the
;; provisioner said so, not because anyone chose it. The per-Bot fields
;; already existed and nothing ever varied them.
;;
;; ## A profile carries no authority, and that is enforced
;;
;; A profile may name a provider, a model and a cadence. It may NOT name
;; capabilities, tools, scopes, writes, approvals or accounts. Authority has
;; one path — loop-yakuwari's `:yakuwari/capabilities`, carried as a biscuit,
;; decided by `kotoba-lang/authority` — and a second surface that could widen
;; a Bot's reach is exactly the thing ADR-2608180200 refuses.
;;
;; `awai.registry/validate-fleet` rejects an authority-shaped key here rather
;; than ignoring it: ignoring would let someone write `:profile/tools` and
;; believe it had an effect.
;;
;; ## Today every role resolves to :default
;;
;; Landing this changes no Bot's behaviour, deliberately. Which roles should
;; run somewhere else is a cost decision — `claude` draws on a Claude Code
;; subscription, `codex` on another — and it belongs to whoever pays, not to
;; the commit that makes the choice expressible.
;;
;; `:yakuwari/runners` has said `:claude` or `:codex` per role for 63 roles
;; and the fleet has never read it. That is the choice this file makes
;; sayable; it does not make it.

{:awai.profiles/version 1

 :awai.profiles/profiles
 {:default
  {:profile/id :default
   :profile/provider "murakumo"
   :profile/model "murakumo-main"
   :profile/why "The fleet's own inference. One production slot, no external
                 billing, and the only provider every Bot can use without a
                 subscription question. What provisioning hardcoded."}

  ;; Declared and unused. Kept because a profile nobody can name is a profile
  ;; nobody can choose, and the point of this file is that the choice becomes
  ;; visible rather than buried in a literal.
  :claude-subscription
  {:profile/id :claude-subscription
   :profile/provider "claude-bridge"
   :profile/model "claude-sonnet-5"
   :profile/why "Claude Code subscription via the local bridge on 127.0.0.1:9180.
                 Assigning a role here spends a subscription rather than the
                 fleet's own hardware, which is why no role is assigned by
                 this commit."}}

 ;; role kind -> profile. An absent kind resolves to :default.
 :awai.profiles/by-role {}

 ;; A single role may override its kind. Empty for the same reason.
 :awai.profiles/by-key
 ;; The 20 authored-work stewards run on the Claude subscription rather than
 ;; the fleet's own hardware.
 ;;
 ;; Not because they are more important -- because they are the roles closest
 ;; to the thing the fleet has never done. In 670 runs it has produced zero
 ;; approval cards, zero patches and zero artifacts, and these are the roles
 ;; that own a published work.
 ;;
 ;; It also relieves the murakumo slot, which is the actual failure source:
 ;; measured 2026-08-20, two thirds of runs failed, uniformly across every
 ;; role, because all 90 contend for ONE slot at parallel:1. Nothing about
 ;; that rate is a property of any role.
 ;;
 ;; Cost is bounded and stated: 20 roles at 1440-minute cadence is 20 calls a
 ;; day. The heavier contention is the 24 roles at 360 minutes (96 calls a
 ;; day); moving those would relieve more and cost more, and that is a
 ;; separate decision by whoever pays.
 ;;
 ;; Listed one per line rather than selected by job, because `by-key` is keyed
 ;; by the projection's key and each of these has a distinct kind
 ;; (:work-hagane, :work-isekai, ...). `validate-fleet` refuses any entry that
 ;; matches no role, so a typo here fails rather than sits silent.
 {
  "animeka/work-hagane" :claude-subscription
  "animeka/work-isekai" :claude-subscription
  "animeka/work-konbi" :claude-subscription
  "animeka/work-nyacat" :claude-subscription
  "animeka/work-ramen" :claude-subscription
  "animeka/work-sakura" :claude-subscription
  "animeka/work-shiropico" :claude-subscription
  "animeka/work-toshi" :claude-subscription
  "dougaka/work-catalog" :claude-subscription
  "gameka/work-survivors-zombie" :claude-subscription
  "gameka/work-survivors-zombie-mall" :claude-subscription
  "mangaka/work-ghost-hacker" :claude-subscription
  "mangaka/work-ghostmass" :claude-subscription
  "mangaka/work-halfgram" :claude-subscription
  "mangaka/work-yamainu" :claude-subscription
  "mangaka/work-zankyo" :claude-subscription
  "yukkuri/channel-anime" :claude-subscription
  "yukkuri/channel-cyber" :claude-subscription
  "yukkuri/channel-pachinko" :claude-subscription
  "yukkuri/channel-truecrime" :claude-subscription}}
